Z||000000||87ECO5||04-20-2001||03:37 PM||||Can I post a vague question like this?  Generally speaking, what methods best teach you discipline?||||reg||5
Z||000001||WampusCat||04-20-2001||04:13 PM||||Umm....join the Marine Corps?  Visit a dominatrix?  It is kind of a vague question.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||04-20-2001||04:23 PM||||Are you talking raising kids, or like military discipline?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Well, I'm 20... but whenever I was really yelled at when I was younger, that just got me more pi$$ed off and instantly "hated" that person.  As far as my parents go, if I ever did something "not right" they'd just explain to me why I shouldn't do whatever it was that I did.  No hitting, no "grounding", whatever.. just explaining, and I would get the hint the first time.  Of course, I seem to have more common sense than most other people my age that I've been friends with, so maybe that has something to do with it.<P>My grandparents always thought that my parents should've spanked me any time I did something wrong and that I should go to church... (they're very strict Catholics if that has anything to do with it).  But it seems that I came out fine... can't say the same for my cousins though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||04-20-2001||08:05 PM||||I think its different for every person.  <P>Some people can just be yelled at or have priveleges taken away from them, and that will work.  Others need a smack or two.  I was one of the ones who needed a smack every once in a while.  I can honestly tell you if my parents didn't discipline me like that I would probably be a juvenile delinquent (in a riced out Civic too! even worse).  They tried to do it the "nice" way but I would find ways around it (like they took my TV away so I listened to my stereo, then they took that away so I listened to my walkman etc.) and actions speak louder then words.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000004||deceler8||04-20-2001||09:04 PM||||May not be the answer you're looking for, but sacrifice and self-denial are the only ways to teach yourself discipline.<P>You don't have to have stuff to be a viable human being...the trick is knowing what you need is different from what you want. <P>Sure, I'd like a Corvette and I probably could afford one, but the decision to buy one  probably wouldn't change my life in any meaningful way. Besides, Corvettes are for the balding middle-age crowd. Fieros, on the other hand...||||reg||1
Z||000005||KnightRyder31||04-21-2001||01:43 PM||||Martial Arts.<BR>It taught me a great deal of discipline and respect for myself and others.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||04-21-2001||06:05 PM||||Knightryder's right. Martial arts. Pick one that fits your lifestyle. Not all of them are supremely high-impact, and you don't need to compete to get good. I take Hapkido. It's great.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||04-21-2001||08:26 PM||||9 1/5 years of both Aikido and Ju Jitsu...and loved every minute of it! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||04-22-2001||03:33 PM|||| Discipline is far different than punishment. Discipline requires intense personal introspection. Discipline is doing what "NEEDS" to be done above all else. When you are required to follow a specific proccess or perform a certain function for the good of the whole, you do it whithout regard to self. Discipline as used in terms of punishment is an attemp to bring about conformity through physical or tangible sanctions. Discipline is tought, but only the willing can truly bennefit. As mentioned before, everybodies sense of discipline varries. Please do not confuse, as many do, discipline with punishment. They are to different animals. I have never formaly engaged in martial arts training, but I do understand the sense of mutal human respect and self respect that is a the major bennefit of MA training. I know just enough about it get my self in trouble someday. But it's like I always,always say; "Treat those around you as you would have them treat you". Discipline is ones inner strenght to combat through adversity and reach the goal. Concentration fueld by direction and purpose aided by inner stength and determination, follwed by sense of completion and wellbeing. "You have learned well Grasshopper". <P>Peace be unto you my friends   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||6
